course: dictionary
lesson: 12298
title: Working together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cooperation means working together with other people to reach the same goal. «The class showed great cooperation when they built a tower out of paper cups.» Everyone helped, so the tower got finished.
explain: Cooperation can also mean being helpful and doing what you are asked. «Thank you for your cooperation» is what a teacher or police officer might say when people follow their instructions.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. Words like together, team and helped point to cooperation. Check your meaning by swapping in «working together» and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Cooperation is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «good cooperation», not «a cooperation».
fact: «Cooperation» means working together with other people to reach the same goal.
fact: «Cooperation» can also mean being helpful and doing what you are asked.
fact: Ants show cooperation when they carry food back to the nest together.
fact: «International cooperation» means countries sharing work, like the International Space Station.
exercise: «Our team showed real cooperation, and we won the relay race.» What does cooperation mean here? | Arguing about the rules | Running as fast as you can alone | Eating lunch quickly | *Working together to reach the same goal
exercise: «Thank you for your cooperation, children, the bell has gone.» What does cooperation mean here? | Shouting loudly | *Doing what you are asked | Forgetting your bag | Being late for class
exercise: Which phrase means countries sharing their work? | Thank you for your help | Dark night | Hot weather | *International cooperation
test: «The wolves hunted together, and their cooperation helped them catch a deer.» What does cooperation mean here? | *Working together to catch food | Sleeping in the sun | Running away from the pack | Hiding from other animals
test: «Our school project was done in cooperation with the local library.» What does «in cooperation with» mean? | Far away from | Instead of | Against | *Working together with
exam: Which sentence shows cooperation? | The rain stopped suddenly | The children argued and sat apart | Nobody came to school today | *The children took turns and helped each other tidy the room
